\subsection{8.3 Toward a Futarchy of Fields}
Robin Hansonâ€™s futarchy proposed separating values (what we want to maximize) from beliefs (which policies will achieve them) \citep{hanson2003}. Citizens vote on values, while prediction markets decide policies. However, wealth-dominated markets risk plutocracy. RSVP-based futarchy retools this as field feedback governance, employing distributed deliberation networksâ€”rotating citizen assemblies, local expertise pools, and community panelsâ€”to forecast policy impacts \citep{ortega1957}. Policies are chosen by their predicted effect on the field: smoothing gradients, reducing entropy, and reinforcing coherence.
