ass="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="frac-line" style="border-bottom-width: 0.04em;"></span></span><span style="top: -3.485em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mopen mtight">âŸ¨</span><span class="mord mtight">Î¦</span><span class="mclose mtight"><span class="mclose mtight">âŸ©</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8913em;"><span style="top: -2.931em; margin-right: 0.0714em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.5em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size3 size1 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">â€‹</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.52em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose nulldelimiter"></span></span></span></span></span>. Roadmap spans prototypes to public demos.</li>
</ul>
<h4 dir="auto" class="">Part IV: Implications and Futures</h4>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Explores broader ramifications.</p>
<ul dir="auto" class="marker:text-secondary">
<li class="break-words"><strong class="font-semibold">Chapter 11: Philosophical Horizons of the Plenum</strong>
Aligns RSVP with process philosophy (Deleuze &amp; Guattari, 1987; Whitehead, 1978), reframing persons as field nodes and coherence as a moral value <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>min</mi><mo>â¡</mo><mtext>â€‰</mtext><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">V</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">a</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Î¦</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J = \min \, \mathrm{Var}(\Phi)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.09618em;">J</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mop">min</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathrm">Var</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">Î¦</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span>.</li>
<li class="break-words"><strong class="font-semibold">Chapter 12: Ethics and Political Economy in RSVP</strong>
Entropic ethics minimizes variance; critiques colonial/patriarchal distortions. Economics smooths gradients via policy levers.</li>
<li class="break-words"><strong class="font-semibold">Chapter 13: Empirical Predictions and Testing</strong>
Cosmological (e.g., CMB anomalies), neurocognitive (fMRI coherence), and social predictions (e.g., geozotic stability). Falsifiability criteria provided.</li>
<li class="break-words"><strong class="font-semibold">Chapter 14: RSVP and Artificial Intelligence</strong>
HYDRA/TARTAN for modular AI; alignment via futarchy; consciousness as field coherence.</li>
<li class="break-words"><strong class="font-semibold">Chapter 15: Futures of Society and Consciousness</strong>
Envisions post-individualist attractors, governance by coherence, and AI as plenum participants.</li>
<li class="break-words"><strong class="font-semibold">Epilogue: The Rise of Coherence</strong>
Synthesizes the arc: from physics to society, emphasizing distributed agency over isolation.</li>
</ul>
<h4 dir="auto" class="">Appendices</h4>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Provide derivations (e.g., field equations in A), sparse projections (B), categories (C), architectures (D, H), economics (E), cosmology (F), implementations (G), and extended HYDRA/TARTAN formalism (H, including stability proofs).</p>
<h4 dir="auto" class="">Bibliography and Overall Assessment</h4>
