\subsection*{12.6 Conclusion}
Ethics and economics converge in RSVP as coherence. Colonialism and patriarchy fractured fields; neoliberalism amplifies distortions. Entropic ethics repairs them by diffusing stress and embedding individuals in resilient clusters \citep{deleuze1987}. This sets the stage for empirical testing (Chapter 13).
\section*{Chapter 13: Empirical Predictions and Testing}
RSVP is not only a philosophical or mathematical exercise. It proposes to be a scientific theory---one that can be tested, falsified, and refined \citep{jaynes2003}. Its claims span cosmology, cognition, and social organization. This chapter sketches empirical avenues where RSVP can be tested, identifying measurable predictions and research programs \citep{baez2011}.
\subsection*{13.1 Cosmological Predictions}
RSVP challenges the <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Î›</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord">Î›</span></span></span></span>CDM model by replacing cosmic expansion with entropic smoothing (Appendix F) \citep{whitehead1978}. Testable predictions include:
\begin{itemize}
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\item \textbf{Redshift Integral}: Redshift is reinterpreted as entropic diffusion, predicting deviations from the linear Hubble law at large distances \citep{gromov1999}.
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\item \textbf{CMB Anomalies}: RSVP anticipates coherence patterns in the CMB, detectable as non-random alignments in multipole modes \citep{baez2011}.
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\item \textbf{Structure Formation}: Smoother void profiles and less pronounced dark matter halos compared to <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Î›</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord">Î›</span></span></span></span>CDM simulations \citep{whitehead1978}.
\end{itemize}
